[color=#ff0000][size=6][b]OFFLINE ONLY[/b][/size][/color]
[size=4][b]This mod is UNOFFICIAL.[/b] It is not affiliated with the ERR team, the Convergence Team, or the ERTE author, and they don't support it.
Do [b]NOT[/b] ask for help in the official ERR, Convergence or ERTE channels while this mod is installed. Remove it first, then check whether your problem is still there. I am not responsible if you get kicked or banned.
For questions and bug reports - join our [url=https://discord.gg/JvTMwPCygB][b]Discord server[/b][/url][/size]

[size=5][b]Compatible with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/510]Seamless Co-op[/url][/b][/size]

[size=4][b]Description[/b][/size]
[color=#D4D4D8]DLL version[/color] of the Map for Goblins mod. Thousands of loot and world icons on the in-game map, and [b]no regulation.bin changes[/b]: all map data gets injected into memory at runtime, so it won't conflict with other mods that edit the regulation.

There are plenty of builds on the Files tab, pick the one for your game:
[list]
[*][b]Vanilla version[/b], for the base game + Shadow of the Erdtree. ~6900 icons, same mod, just without the ERR-only categories. Also works with the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/428]Item & Enemy Randomizer[/url] - see below.[/*]
[*][b]ERR version[/b], for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/541]ERR[/url]. ~9100 icons, including the ERR-specific stuff (Rune Pieces, Ember Pieces, Kindling Spirits, unique loot etc).[/*]
[*][b]Convergence version[/b], for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/3419]The Convergence[/url] (3.x, runs on ModEngine3 / me3), ~8100 icons, so it covers its relocated loot, new bosses and reworked zones.[/*]
[*][b]ERTE version[/b], for [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/2747]ERTE[/url], ~8000 icons.[/*]
[*][b]Golden Age version[/b], for the [url=https://soulsmods.com/mods/cmkst0a23000009jlzm0f1jvs/elden-ring-golden-age-overhaul-mod]Elden Ring Golden Age[/url] overhaul, ~7100 icons.[/*]
[*][b]ELDEN VINS version[/b], for the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/4709]ELDEN VINS[/url] overhaul, ~7500 icons.[/*]
[*][b]Elden Ring Reborn version[/b], for the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/2202]Elden Ring Reborn[/url] overhaul, ~7100 icons.[/*]
[*][b]Graceborne version[/b], for the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/5207]Graceborne[/url] Bloodborne-inspired overhaul (runs on Mod Engine 3 / me3), ~7100 icons.[/*]
[/list]
[i]Each build is locked to the game/overhaul version it was generated from; after a major update to that game or overhaul, grab the matching MapForGoblins build.[/i]
Based on [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/3091]Map for Goblins[/url] by Harmonixer and [url=https://github.com/Gacsam/Goblin-ERR]Goblin-ERR[/url] by Gacsam, rebuilt from scratch as a [b]single DLL[/b] - the icons are injected into the map at runtime, so the mod ships no gfx and modifies no game files.

[size=5][color=#ff8c00][b]Install is just one DLL[/b][/color][/size]
This is a pure DLL: the only files are [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] (kept together). All icon categories are [b]ON by default[/b] - open the ini, or press [b][color=#ff8c00]F10[/color][/b] (or [b][color=#ff8c00]Y+R3[/color][/b] on a controller) in-game, to turn off any you don't want.
[b]Updating from an older version?[/b] This version no longer uses a gfx file. After replacing the DLL, [color=#ff8c00]delete the old 02_120_worldmap.gfx[/color] (the old "menu" folder, and for ERR the "addons\MapForGoblins" folder) and remove any old "mods"/"packages" entry that pointed at the MapForGoblins asset folder - only the DLL needs to be registered now.

[size=5][color=#ff8c00][b]In-game mod menu[/b][/color][/size]
[img]https://staticdelivery.nexusmods.com/mods/4333/images/10062/10062-1783098972-301371669.png[/img]
Press [b][color=#ff8c00]F10[/color][/b] (keyboard) or [b][color=#ff8c00]Y+R3[/color][/b] (controller) to open a settings panel right inside the game - no more alt-tabbing to edit the ini. From it you can:
[list]
[*]Turn any icon category on or off, or use [b]Show all[/b] / [b]Hide all[/b] at once[/*]
[*]Flip the master "Show map icons" switch[/*]
[*]Adjust the [b]overlay text size[/b] with a slider - handy on 4K / high-DPI screens[/*]
[*]Copy a marker dump for bug reports[/*]
[/list]
[b]Toggling a category takes effect right away on the open map[/b] - its icons appear or disappear without closing the map. (Some other options, such as spoiler-free mode, apply the next time you open the map.) Mouse, keyboard and controller supported.

[size=4][b]Main features[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]In-game mod menu[/b] (see above): F10 (or Y+R3 on a controller) opens a settings panel to toggle icon categories, the master switch and Show all / Hide all without editing the ini. Category toggles take effect right away on the open map.[/*]
[*]Icon categories that can be turned on/off individually in [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b]: weapons, armour, talismans, spells, key items, smithing stones, gloveworts, cookbooks, bell bearings, gathering nodes, bosses, graces, stakes of Marika, spirit springs, imp statues, paintings, summoning pools, map fragments, gestures, NPC invaders, puzzles etc.[/*]
[*]Icons in a region only show up after you've found that region's map fragment (can be disabled).[/*]
[*]Things you've already collected disappear from the map: including gathered material nodes (like Arteria Leaf), Rune/Ember Pieces etc. Defeated bosses either hide or get a checkmark (configurable).[/*]
[*]Every marker shows its location name, down to sub-areas (like Siofra Aqueduct/Siofra River etc). The mod uses original game strings, everything should be localised out of the box.[/*]
[*]The INI maintains itself. If there's no file - it gets created. If there are new options after an update - they will be added automatically.[/*]
[*]Master on/off for all icons: the "Show map icons" switch in the overlay, or [b]F10[/b] / [b]Y+R3[/b] directly when the overlay is turned off in the ini.[/*]
[*][b]Item & Enemy Randomizer support[/b] (vanilla build, on by default): loot markers read the loaded regulation at startup, so each one shows the item that's [i]actually[/i] there - right name, right icon - and disappears when you pick up the real light point. Works with any seed, no per-seed setup. Turn it off in the ini if you play vanilla without the randomizer.[/*]
[*][b]Spoiler-free mode[/b] (optional, set anonymous_loot in the ini): every loot marker shows a plain "?" icon and a generic label instead of the real item, so you can find loot without knowing what it is - made for blind / randomizer runs.[/*]
[*]The ERR version can optionally tie ERR's own pre-placed markers (camps, merchants, bosses, dungeon entrances) to the same display rules as this mod's icons, so everything on the map follows one logic: show after map discovery, hide once cleared. If you prefer ERR's markers as they are, turn these options off in the ini.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b]Installation - ERR version[/b][/size]
[spoiler]
[list=1]
[*]Download the ERR file and unpack it[/*]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into your ERR [b]dll\offline\[/b] folder[/*]
[*]Launch through ERR as usual[/*]
[/list]
Settings are in [b]dll\offline\MapForGoblins.ini[/b] - all categories are ON by default, turn off what you don't want (or use F10 in-game).[/spoiler]

[size=4][b]Installation - Vanilla version[/b][/size]
You need a mod loader, either [b]ModEngine3 (me3)[/b] or [b]ModEngine2[/b].

[b]Option A: ModEngine3 (me3), recommended[/b]
[spoiler]
[list=1]
[*]Install me3 ([url=https://github.com/garyttierney/me3/releases]me3_installer.exe[/url], docs at [url=https://me3.help/]me3.help[/url])[/*]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] next to your .me3 profile (e.g. eldenring-default.me3)[/*]
[*]Open the .me3 profile in Notepad and make sure it has:
[code]profileVersion = "v1"

[[supports]]
game = "eldenring"

[[natives]]
path = 'MapForGoblins.dll'[/code]
[/*]
[*]Double-click the .me3 file to play[/*]
[/list]
[/spoiler]
[b]Option B: ModEngine2[/b]
[spoiler]
[list=1]
[*]Get [url=https://github.com/soulsmods/ModEngine2/releases]ModEngine2[/url] and extract it anywhere (NOT into the game folder)[/*]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into the ModEngine2 directory (next to launchmod_eldenring.bat)[/*]
[*]In [b]config_eldenring.toml[/b], under [modengine], register the DLL:
[code]external_dlls = [ "MapForGoblins.dll" ][/code]
[/*]
[*]Run launchmod_eldenring.bat[/*]
[/list]
[/spoiler]
[b]Option C: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/117]Elden Mod Loader[/url][/b] [i](simple DLL loader)[/i]
[spoiler]
This mod is a plain DLL, so it loads through Elden Mod Loader like any other DLL mod.
[list=1]
[*]Install Elden Mod Loader (by techiew): extract its files into your [b]Game[/b] folder (next to eldenring.exe) - it adds dinput8.dll, mod_loader_config.ini and a [b]mods[/b] folder[/*]
[*][b]Open mod_loader_config.ini and set [color=#ff0000]load_delay = 0[/color][/b] - EML's default delay (e.g. 5000 = 5s) loads the DLL after the world map is already built, so the icons will not appear. Setting it to 0 loads the DLL early enough to inject the icons[/*]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into that [b]mods[/b] folder (EML loads every DLL in there at startup)[/*]
[*]Launch the game offline (EML does not bypass EAC, so play offline)[/*]
[/list]
[/spoiler]
[b]Option D: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/5998]Mod Engine 2 with Lazy Loader[/url][/b] [i](popular on Steam Deck)[/i]
[spoiler]
Same as ModEngine2, but its config lives in the [b]base/[/b] folder.
[list=1]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into the main [b]Game[/b] folder (next to eldenring.exe)[/*]
[*]Open [b]base/config.toml[/b] and add the DLL to external_dlls:
[code]external_dlls = [
    "MapForGoblins.dll"
][/code]
[/*]
[*]Launch from eldenring.exe as usual[/*]
[/list]
The DLL must be in [b]external_dlls[/b]: Lazy Loader only loads ModEngine from base/, it does not auto-inject mod DLLs.[/spoiler]
Settings are in [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] - all categories are ON by default, turn off what you don't want (or use F10 in-game).

[size=4][b]Using it with the Item & Enemy Randomizer[/b][/size]
Use the [b]Vanilla version[/b]. Install it the same way (ModEngine3/me3 or ModEngine2), alongside the randomizer's generated [b]regulation.bin[/b] in your load order. Nothing else to set up: the live-loot options are [b]on by default[/b] in the vanilla build, so at startup the markers read your loaded seed and show the real item (name + icon) and hide on the actual light-point pickup. For a blind run, set [b]anonymous_loot = true[/b] in the ini to replace every loot marker with a "?" and a generic label.

[size=4][b]Installation - Convergence version (3.x, ModEngine3 / me3)[/b][/size]
[spoiler]
Convergence 3.x launches through a [b].me3[/b] profile in ConvergenceER\me3 (convergence.me3, and convergence - seamless.me3 if you use Seamless Co-op).
[list=1]
[*]Download the Convergence 3.x file and unpack it[/*]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into [b]...\ConvergenceER\mod\dll[/b] (next to ErdTools.dll, erdyes.dll, etc.)[/*]
[*]Open the [b].me3[/b] profile you launch with in Notepad and add the DLL as a native:
[code][[natives]]
path = './../mod/dll/MapForGoblins.dll'[/code]
[/*]
[*]Launch through Start_Convergence.bat as usual[/*]
[/list]
Settings are in [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] - all categories ON by default (turn off what you don't want, or use F10).[/spoiler]

[size=4][b]Installation - ERTE version[/b][/size]
[spoiler]
ERTE runs on [b]Mod Engine 3 (me3)[/b] through its .me3 profile (e.g. eldenring-ERTE-SOTE-CoopReady.me3).
[list=1]
[*]Download the ERTE file and unpack it[/*]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into a "MapForGoblins" folder next to ERTE's mod folder, i.e. into [b]...\me3\config\profiles\eldenring-mods\MapForGoblins\[/b] (alongside the "ERTE SOTE" folder)[/*]
[*]Open the ERTE [b].me3[/b] profile in Notepad and add the DLL as a native:
[code][[natives]]
path = 'eldenring-mods\MapForGoblins\MapForGoblins.dll'[/code]
[/*]
[*]Launch through the ERTE .me3 profile as usual[/*]
[/list]
Settings are in [b]MapForGoblins\MapForGoblins.ini[/b] - all categories ON by default (turn off what you don't want, or use F10).[/spoiler]

[size=4][b]Installation - Golden Age / ELDEN VINS / Elden Ring Reborn (ModEngine2)[/b][/size]
[spoiler]
These three overhauls each ship their own [b]ModEngine2[/b], so the steps are identical - only the folder and the launch .bat differ.
[list=1]
[*]Download the file for your overhaul and unpack it[/*]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into the overhaul's folder (next to its config_eldenring.toml and its launch .bat)[/*]
[*]In [b]config_eldenring.toml[/b] add the DLL to external_dlls:
[code]external_dlls = [
    ...existing entries...,
    "MapForGoblins.dll",
][/code]
[/*]
[*]Launch via that overhaul's usual .bat[/*]
[/list]
Launch file per overhaul:
[list]
[*][b]Golden Age[/b]: Start_GoldenAge.bat[/*]
[*][b]ELDEN VINS[/b]: Launch ELDEN VINS.bat[/*]
[*][b]Elden Ring Reborn[/b]: Click To Play Reborn!.bat[/*]
[/list]
Settings are in [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] - all categories ON by default (turn off what you don't want, or use F10).[/spoiler]

[size=4][b]Installation - Graceborne (Mod Engine 3 / me3)[/b][/size]
[spoiler]
Graceborne launches through its [b].me3[/b] profile (launch.me3) and serves the mod from its [b]mod[/b] folder.
[list=1]
[*]Download the Graceborne file and unpack it[/*]
[*]Copy [b]MapForGoblins.dll[/b] and [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] into Graceborne's [b]mod[/b] folder, i.e. [b]...\GRACEBORNE\mod\[/b] (next to regulation.bin and Scripts-Data-Exposer-FS.dll)[/*]
[*]Open [b]launch.me3[/b] in a text editor and add the DLL as a native (anywhere among the [[natives]] entries):
[code][[natives]]
path = 'mod/MapForGoblins.dll'[/code]
[/*]
[*]Launch via Graceborne's usual .me3 launcher[/*]
[/list]
Settings are in [b]MapForGoblins.ini[/b] - all categories ON by default (turn off what you don't want, or use F10).[/spoiler]

[size=4][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Vanilla version: a DLL loader - [url=https://github.com/garyttierney/me3/releases]ModEngine3[/url], [url=https://github.com/soulsmods/ModEngine2/releases]ModEngine2[/url], or [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/117]Elden Mod Loader[/url][/*]
[*]ERR version: [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/541]ERR[/url] itself, nothing else. The mod loads through ERR's own loader.[/*]
[*]Convergence version: an installed [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/3419]The Convergence[/url] (3.x, runs on ModEngine3 / me3). Shadow of the Erdtree is required by the overhaul itself.[/*]
[*]ERTE version: an installed [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/2747]ERTE[/url] (it runs on Mod Engine 3). Shadow of the Erdtree is required by the overhaul itself.[/*]
[*][url=https://soulsmods.com/mods/cmkst0a23000009jlzm0f1jvs/elden-ring-golden-age-overhaul-mod]Golden Age[/url] / [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/4709]ELDEN VINS[/url] / [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/2202]Elden Ring Reborn[/url] versions: the matching overhaul installed (each ships its own ModEngine2). Shadow of the Erdtree is required by the overhauls themselves.[/*]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/5207]Graceborne[/url] version: an installed Graceborne (Bloodborne-inspired; runs on Mod Engine 3 / me3). Shadow of the Erdtree is required by the overhaul itself.[/*]
[*][color=#ff0000][b]OFFLINE ONLY.[/b][/color] Mod loaders disable EAC, so the "Inappropriate activity detected" message at launch is normal.[/*]
[/list]

